codex
The canonical inventory contains five rules, all with empty attribute lists. Stage 1 compiles all five into `VERIFICATION` before either positive `kprove` command; it never first proves any rule’s exact statement in a rule-free module. The mutation checks are rejection probes, not derived-lemma proofs. On the rule bodies themselves, all five are defining equations, so the derived-lemma and domain-lemma sets are empty.
